# A generated JSON file must never be text-merged. On 14/08/2026 `-X theirs`
# stitched a counts header from one generation onto rows from another in
# data/company-awards.json, and only the publish gate caught it. Marking the
# file -merge makes git REFUSE rather than stitch; the workflow then re-derives
# it (scripts/refresh_company_press.py --merge), which is the documented fix.
data/company-press.json -merge

# Same reasoning, added 28/08/2026 with the MHRA alerts refresh workflow.
# refresh_mhra_alerts.py rebuilds this file additively against origin's latest
# copy on a push conflict (git fetch + reset --hard + rerun) rather than ever
# text-merging it — -merge makes that the only path git will allow.
data/mhra-alerts.json -merge

# Same reasoning, added 08/09/2026 with the private provider moves tracker
# (page 1666, Hub build 3/3). refresh_private_provider_moves.py rebuilds this
# file additively against origin's latest copy on a push conflict, same as
# mhra-alerts.json above.
data/private-provider-moves.json -merge
